@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.TeamAxelModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Axel Marcellino Antonio";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <div class="event-hero reveal">
            <div class="event-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Our Team</p>
                <h2>Axel Marcellino Antonio</h2>

                <p class="event-intro">
                    A Deaf staff member who brings joy into every interaction—
                    through service, energy, and a strong willingness to grow.
                </p>

                <div class="event-tags">
                    <span>Deaf Staff</span>
                    <span>Service</span>
                    <span>Joyful Energy</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="team-profile-hero-img reveal">
                <img src="/images/team/axel.jpg" alt="Axel Marcellino Antonio">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">His Beginning</p>
                <h3>Starting the Journey</h3>

                <p>
                    Axel started working at Kopi Cinta in December 2023
                    as a Deaf staff member.
                </p>

                <p>
                    He works across multiple stations, including the bar,
                    popcorn, and cotton candy sections.
                </p>

                <p>
                    His role includes preparing drinks, serving customers,
                    and creating small joyful moments—
                    especially for families who visit.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-block-card">
                <h4>His Role</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Bar service</li>
                    <li>Popcorn station</li>
                    <li>Cotton candy station</li>
                    <li>Customer interaction</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-feature reveal">
            <div class="hbii-feature-card">
                <p class="hbii-label">Purpose</p>
                <h3>Choosing Growth and Independence</h3>

                <p>
                    Axel joined Kopi Cinta because it provides inclusive
                    job opportunities for Deaf staff.
                </p>

                <p>
                    He wanted to become more independent, learn new skills,
                    and grow within the service field.
                </p>

                <p>
                    During his time here, he feels happy and proud—
                    supported by an environment where he can communicate
                    and collaborate with the team.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-feature-card soft">
                <p class="hbii-label">Challenge</p>
                <h3>When Communication Feels Different</h3>

                <p>
                    One of the main challenges Axel faces is communication
                    with customers who are not familiar with sign language.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Lip-reading can also be difficult at times,
                    especially depending on how people speak.
                </p>

                <p>
                    But he handles this through writing, gestures,
                    or support from his teammates.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-ending reveal">
            <h3>His Message</h3>

            <p>
                Axel hopes hearing people can be more patient and open
                when communicating with Deaf staff.
            </p>

            <p>
                There is no need to be afraid.
                With simple writing or gestures, we can understand each other.
            </p>

            <p>
                Because for him, communication is not about using the same way—
                but about the willingness to understand.
            </p>
        </div>

        <br />

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Team</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>